0d35cd7-16d2-5639-b617-8a3a49f3ba32" :answer-field/id #uuid "50d35cd7-16d2-5639-b617-8a3a49f3ba32" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["bcb13961-0ed3-52d4-8ecc-3ceca2f3b0d9" "6c49c4ed-34a4-53f5-ab29-0ff60faa4624"] :answer-field/correct "bcb13961-0ed3-52d4-8ecc-3ceca2f3b0d9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4ce2ea85-552c-5e62-a3ef-0a5e7f4819be" :question/id #uuid "4ce2ea85-552c-5e62-a3ef-0a5e7f4819be" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=n\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement II is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["fee93e3b-06c8-5ee1-8dd8-365bfe5b8c36" "3d34c88c-5469-595e-a429-afe7922b5634" "50d35cd7-16d2-5639-b617-8a3a49f3ba32"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a029a29f-51c9-5fa2-a876-4daa2792a47d" :answer/id #uuid "a029a29f-51c9-5fa2-a876-4daa2792a47d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7cce4ff9-d81f-585b-8527-5b41abd3d68c" :answer/id #uuid "7cce4ff9-d81f-585b-8527-5b41abd3d68c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true" :db/ensur